module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unread_arm_missing_on_a_secondary_axis

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unread_arm_missing_on_a_secondary_axis: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unread_arm_missing_on_a_secondary_axis" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A CARRIER THAT MODELS UNREAD ON ITS PRIMARY AXIS AND NOT ON A SECONDARY ONE FORCES EVERY ROW TO ASSERT THE SECONDARY FACT.** The author has no arm for what the source did not say, so an arm that says something must be inhabited, and the resulting row is indistinguishable from one whose source stated the fact outright. The defect is not that the author was careless: it is that the carrier offered no way to be careful, and the type system then certifies the fabrication. ",

    "SPECIMEN (2026-09-09, gunbc colo census, session bright-swift-678). `extdeps.colo.types::CabinetDensityClaim` gets the primary axis exactly right - a figure nobody published is `DensityUnread` carrying an obligation, which is the rule the whole census exists to enforce. The SAME TYPE offers only `DensityMarketedAirOnly` and `DensityMarketedMax` for the COOLING MEDIUM, and neither means `the page did not say`. Two rows whose pages name no medium at all - `njfx_wall_density` and `digital_fortress_piscataway_density` - therefore inhabit the air-only arm, asserting air-cooled capability inferred from the ABSENCE of a liquid claim. That is the census's own cardinal error, committed by the carrier built to prevent it, one axis over. Two more instances were found in another lane the same day, making the population four rows across two sessions. ",

    "**THE HONESTY MIGRATES INTO PROSE, WHICH IS WHERE IT DIES.** Both rows' `citation` strings say plainly that the medium is unread and the arm is a carrier gap. That reads like a fix and is not one: DESIGN section 4c rules that an annotation is never evidence a machine claim holds, because no `Accepted` program can read one, and a `citation` String is worse than an annotation because it is program data that no fold interprets. Review 62888 states the consequence exactly - nothing downstream can distinguish these rows from one whose air arm was selected by the operator's own printed word AIR, which is the distinction the carrier exists to keep. ",

    "AND THE FABRICATION GETS CONSUMED, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES IT MORE THAN A DOCUMENTATION DEFECT. The lane's own witness asserts an established AIR-COOLED watt reading and an air ceiling over one of those rows, so the inferred medium becomes an executing, green, enrolled claim. A prose caveat and a passing witness disagree, and only one of them runs. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: for each axis a carrier's arms decide, ask whether a source that is SILENT on that axis has an arm. If the answer is no on any axis, every row is asserting that axis whether its author meant to or not** - and the tell that this has already happened is a row explaining in prose why its arm is not really a reading. A carrier with an unread arm on one axis is not thereby safe on its neighbours; the correctness of the primary axis is what makes the secondary one invisible, because the author has already been careful once and the type accepted it. ",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS. [[absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked]] is an INSTRUMENT failing to distinguish a miss from an absence; here the instrument read correctly and the CARRIER had nowhere to put the result. [[absence_classifier_default_bucket]] is a classifier whose accepted bucket absorbs unmodeled kinds; here there is no default and no residual - the author is compelled to choose a positive arm, so the fabrication is authored rather than absorbed. [[citation_verified_against_a_rendering_that_destroyed_its_scope]] is a wording attached to the wrong subject; here the wording is correct and complete and the row asserts a fact the wording never carried. ",

    "TRIGGER FIRED 2026-09-10, AND IT DISCHARGED HALF THE CLASS RATHER THAN ALL OF IT. #10888 landed `CoolingMediumStanding = CoolingMediumPublished { medium: CoolingMedium } | CoolingMediumUnspecified`, carried BESIDE the quantity on each figure rather than fused into the claim's arm name. The FORCED half is now structurally impossible: there is no longer any arm an author must inhabit to record a figure whose medium was never published, so the fabrication this class is about cannot be compelled by the carrier. Both specimen rows - `njfx_wall_density` and `digital_fortress_piscataway_density` - are migrated to `CoolingMediumUnspecified` and assert nothing about cooling. ",

    "THE OTHER HALF IS NOT DISCHARGED AND THE ROW WOULD BE INFLATED IF IT CLAIMED OTHERWISE: an author can still WRITE `CoolingMediumPublished { medium: AirCooling }` beside a wording that names no medium. The type offers the honest option; it does not refuse the dishonest one. What changed is that the dishonest one became DECIDABLE, which it was not before - the same carrier added `FigureVerificationStanding` carrying the captured `wording` per figure, so the medium arm and the operator's own sentence now sit in one record and can be compared without refetching anything. Before #10888 the wording lived in a claim-level string shared across figures and there was nothing to compare a per-figure medium against. ",

    "REVISED CEILING AND NEXT TRIGGER, FOR THE SURVIVING HALF: mechanically preventable, reached by a lens asserting that a figure whose medium is `CoolingMediumPublished` carries a `wording` containing a medium term, and that one whose wording names a medium does not sit at `CoolingMediumUnspecified`. Structural impossibility is NOT the ceiling here and claiming it would be dishonest: whether a page names a medium is a fact about external prose, so no constructor can be denied on it - the wall can only compare what was captured against what was asserted, which is validation. The trigger is that lens enrolled in a gate, not authored; an inert lens is itself a lie per DESIGN section 4b. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT (2026-09-09, BEFORE THE CLIMB ABOVE): mitigatable, and only barely - the containment is two prose strings and a review that read them. Nothing prevented the authoring, the compiler accepted it, and a consumer screening candidates on air-cooled density would treat an inferred medium exactly as a published one. ",

    "CEILING AS DERIVED ON 2026-09-09, BEFORE THE CLIMB ABOVE, AND SUPERSEDED BY THE REVISED CEILING RECEIPT: structurally impossible, and the derivation is short. Whether a source stated a cooling medium is DECIDABLE from the capture the row already cites, and the invalid state - a row asserting a medium its source never named - has no constructor once the medium is its own axis with an unstated arm, exactly as the figure axis already is. This is not a predicate lifted to proof; it is one more arm on a coproduct that already has the right shape one axis over. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER AS STATED 2026-09-09; THE CAPABILITY IT NAMES LANDED IN #10888 AND ITS SUFFICIENCY TEST IS HALF MET, WHICH IS WHY THE CLASS STAYS STANDING: a published-medium axis on `CabinetDensityClaim`, orthogonal to the unit and to the direction of the figure, whose arms distinguish a medium the operator PRINTED from one that was never stated - so that a row cannot inhabit an air-cooled reading without a captured wording naming air. It must be SUFFICIENT FOR: no author can record air-cooled capability for a page that says nothing about cooling, and every existing row must be re-decided against its own captured wording rather than defaulted. A carrier that merely adds an `medium_note: String` beside the arm does NOT discharge this - the arm and the note would stay independently writable and one author would satisfy both in a single edit. ",

    "THE 2026-09-09 TRIGGER ADJUDICATED AGAINST ITS OWN SUFFICIENCY CLAUSE, because a trigger is retired by what it named and by nothing else. It named an orthogonal published-medium axis whose arms separate a PRINTED medium from an unstated one: #10888 landed exactly that, `CoolingMediumStanding`, and it is NOT the `medium_note: String` the clause pre-emptively refused, because the unstated case is an ARM rather than an empty string beside an arm. Of the two sufficiency conditions, the second is met - all four read figures in this census were re-decided against their own captured wording, one taking `CoolingMediumPublished { medium: AirCooling }` on the operator's printed word and three taking `CoolingMediumUnspecified`, none defaulted. The first is NOT met: the carrier offers the honest arm without refusing the dishonest one. So the capability half of the trigger is discharged and the class stays Standing on its refusal half, which the revised ceiling above re-triggers as a lens. ",

    "WHY IT RANKS: the rows this corrupts are consumed by cabinet-density screening, and cooling medium is the axis that decides whether a marketed figure is reachable at all for a given deployment. An air reading inferred from silence does not produce an error - it produces a candidate that looks screened. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
